Original commit body from ee30fa9ccf993077562d47c61fdb6ec4a206a1f1:

INV-vilag. run_pytest ended its captured invocation with `|| true`, after
which PIPESTATUS reports the `true` — so `exit_code=${PIPESTATUS[0]}` was
always 0 and pytest's real status was discarded. The verdict was then
reconstructed from the log, which cannot see a collection-error run: pytest
prints ERROR/N errors, never 'FAILED ', so neither failure clause fires while
the affirmative-green clause (N passed && ! N failed) matches. run_pytest
returned 0, the caller's TEST_EXIT -eq 0 gate ran the scoped coverage check
over modules that never imported, and smart-test exited 0 printing a green
checkmark plus a 100%-coverage verdict.

Capture pytest's own status with `|| exit_code=$?` and DELETE the
affirmative-green clause: it was a no-op while exit_code started at 0 and
would mask a real failure now that it does not — the 'latent landmine' the
WI-kalub comment beside it named. The corrective clauses may now only
escalate to failure.

Tests: two behavioral guards sed-extract the real run_pytest from the shipped
script and drive it against a stub pytest, with a positive control proving a
genuinely green run still returns 0. WI-kalub's Step-1b guard is rewritten to
the successor property (exit code sourced from pytest; no PIPESTATUS in code)
because the clause it protected no longer exists.

